mbusgw-t2r (1.4.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * V.01-04ECO07: RAW with RTS/CTS on a USB serial port: the waits for CTS at
    the start of the sessions do not add up when a client reconnects often
    (a session which has come before the end of such a wait does not wait or
    discard anything itself; its data goes behind the data of the one before).

 -- StarLet Squad <zator@yandex.ru>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000

mbusgw-t2r (1.4.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * V.01-04ECO06: RAW with RTS/CTS on a USB serial port: what the previous
    client has left in the adapter is discarded at the start of the next
    session if CTS is off (tried on FTDI only). A session which comes at once
    waits for CTS first, up to iotmo (5 seconds at most) since the end of the
    previous one; the port is opened again then, its input is dropped.
  * A port which cannot be opened a second time (EBUSY, EMFILE) is not closed
    to discard the output: TXNOPURGE instead of DEVLOST.

 -- StarLet Squad <zator@yandex.ru>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

mbusgw-t2r (1.4.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * V.01-04ECO05: USB serial ports with <flow>: a MODBUS request which the line
    has not taken (RTS/CTS), the data dropped by RAWSTALL (RTS/CTS, XON/XOFF)
    are discarded by closing and opening the port; TXNOPURGE tells that it could
    not be done. Tried on FTDI with RTS/CTS only: another chip may keep a part.
  * With RTS/CTS a MODBUS request is not sent while CTS is off (CTSOFF,
    exception 4 after iotmo). A port whose CTS is not wired needs flow = NONE.

 -- StarLet Squad <zator@yandex.ru>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000

